I agree with the suggestion to give to oracle more useful data.  In
addition, I have some...

		More ideas for enhancements to 3.1.3

Someone suggested keeping track of more data for the player, since that is
(after all) what computers are best at.  I'm not a student, like many of
you seem to be, and I have a life, so I can't afford to sit and play
nethack for hours and hours.  If I ever ascend, it will take me days, if
not weeks, to finish the game, a few hours at a time.

For me to keep track of my status, especially between days, I keep a file
of important facts (like where I've seen altars, and how my deity feels
about me now).  It would be nice if "\" showed me some of those things
that I've discovered, and maybe the move number on which I last prayed.
(I'm aware that I can tell about my deity when entering a church or
sacrificing at an altar, but I need one of those to tell.)  Suggested
things to add to the "\" screen:

	What altars I've seen (dungeon, level and God/alignmment).
	Last prayer timestamp. (Control this by an option?  Display it with
				the status info?)
	The tune my deity told me about (such as GCDDB).

Any more?
